l gets her fascination  with material objects from since it was  confirmed that Queen Athena's passing  was the result of a pirate ambush it is  so far-fetched to think that Captain  Hook was the one leading the crusade  after all we all know how much the  pirate hates mermaids of all shapes and  sizes it's only normal for storylines  and animations to change every decade or  so which is why many details may be  different between these 2008 and 1953  Disney films if there's one tidbit that  stayed the same through its a Captain  Hook would travel near and far to put an  end to marine life  this is special this is what what is it  it's a tingle King Triton's hatred for  humans with so many clues pointing  towards Queen Athena being amongst the  mermaids in Peter Pan it's a given that  fans are still questioning this theory  from the very moment we were introduced  to Ariel in the Little Mermaid it became  obvious that she was different than the  rest of her sisters while this set her  apart from them it also caused King  Triton a significant amount of grief as  the ruler of Atlantica King Triton has  to protect the merpeople in his kingdom  sadly he was unable to shield his wife  from her face with this in mind it's  easy to understand why he's so hard on  his youngest daughter Ariel who is  undeniably obsessed with breaking the  rules while King Triton considers  himself to be a reasonable mermaid the  last thing he wants is for his daughters  to get close to human beings this has  everything to do with protecting the  secret world of Atlantica however there  is one underlying reason why King Triton  hates humans more than anything else in  the ocean and this is due to them being  the reason Queen Athena was taken away  from him holding on to such a grudge is  a hard thing to do when your youngest  daughter refuses to keep her distance  from humans after marrying Prince Erik  and giving birth to melody Ariel's  father was finally able to realize that  all humans are evil but this won't stop  him from hating pirates for the rest of  his life Ariel was following in her  mother's footsteps being fascinated with  humans isn't exactly healthy when you're  a mermaid this is a hard truth Ariel  came to know by heart but hey it never  stopped her from approaching the enemy  Ariel spends most of her young life  escaping her Kingdom and swimming up for  air  where she eventually became infatuated  with human life despite her father's  warnings Ariel continued to pay little  minds the dangers surrounding her  King Triton eventually got tired of  Ariel's disobedience but in a way he  also grew to be a bit proud of her -  after all she was following in her  mother's footsteps when it comes to  rules and limitations  Ariel isn't one to abide by them which  is a trait she inherited from Queen  Athena and not King Triton after losing  his wife King Triton did everything he  could to keep his seven daughters out of  harm's way  unfortunately keeping his eyes on them  24 hours a day was just impossible but  without good reason the King does have  to rule Atlantica after all Ariel is the  spitting image of her mother but she  also has her spirit knowing this it  isn't too hard to place  Ariel's mother amongst the mermaids in  Peter Pan it's easy to think of Queen  Athena as a peaceful ruler but if she's  anything like the mermaid in Peter Pan  she's the furthest thing from sweet and  innocent could it be that Queen Athena  lived a double life outside of Atlantica  because it sure looks like she did the  unnamed mermaid with so many Disney  Easter eggs to sift through it can be  challenging to bring the truth to light  this is especially true when taking old  Disney movies into account since Peter  Pan came out nearly 70 years ago some  fan theories can get taken out of  context but before you go and discount  this Peter Pan Easter Egg allow us to  explain since Queen Athena and Princess  Ariel are a lot alike it makes sense  that they would hide